{
  "FUNCTION": {
    "2205D5979E85C7ED": {
      "code_hash": "780f7ba917651f7c59fbc2dc2d42d7f6",
      "code_analysis": "This C/C++ function, `collocate_class_vtable`, primarily consolidates a class's virtual table (vtable) and data structure into a single special VM object. It modifies the owner pointer of all methods within this newly created vtable-data combined object to point at it. The method and field pointers are also adjusted accordingly. Finally, the original class is freed. This function appears to be part of a larger system related to managing objects in memory for a virtual machine (VM).",
      "summary": "The `collocate_class_vtable` function consolidates a class's vtable and data structure into a single special VM object, adjusting owner pointers of all methods within this newly created object to point at it. It also adjusts method and field pointers accordingly before freeing the original class. This function is part of a system related to managing objects in memory for a virtual machine and is called by functions responsible for loading classes from media or an array."
    },
    "3C325C9C8E507630": {
