      "code_analysis": "The function `java_instanceof_class` checks if a given class is an instance of another class or an interface. It does this by comparing the flags and structure of the classes, as well as checking if there are any superclasses that match the target class.",
      "summary": "The high-level purpose of the `java_instanceof_class` function/method is to determine if a given Java class or interface instance belongs to another specified class or interface by comparing its flags and structure, as well as checking for any superclasses that match the target class. This function plays a crucial role in Java Native Interface (JNI) related operations and can be used to verify whether input objects are cast to certain classes, allocate memory for new exceptions, check if two `korp_class` objects are subclasses of each other, or copy elements from one Java array to another among others."
    },
