      "code_analysis": "This C/C++ function calculates the size of a virtual machine (VM) object based on its header. It first gets the value from the header using `GET_VM_OBJ_SIZE_H()`, and then checks if the header is an array, in which case it calculates the size by considering the type of the array, length of elements, and overhead. If not an array, it returns the size calculated for the instance.",
      "summary": "This C++ method calculates the size of a virtual machine (VM) object based on its header and allocates memory for korp_object using GET_VM_OBJ_SIZE_H(). It returns the allocated object pointer which is used to initialize `obj_info` with given header in collocate_class_vtable. The method consolidates vtable and data structure into a single VM object, updates owner pointers of methods within it, modifies field pointers and frees original class."
