      "summary": "The high-level purpose of this C++ function or method is to initialize a binary encoding for a given `kmethod` object and return a boolean value indicating its success or failure. It helps facilitate JIT (Just-In-Time) compilation by generating a stub, allocating memory, and jumping to the compiled target method's address. This enables efficient execution of the targeted function, ensuring optimal performance in an application context."
