    "3C3F0974368E57DA": {
      "code_hash": "2d2d3818ebbda939fb339f4bf9adaf07",
      "code_analysis": "The function is a jump instruction generator based on given target address and mode. It modifies the buffer pointer by incrementing it, depending on the input mode (i_b, i_d, r_d or m_d) and then returns the modified pointer. If the input mode is TARGET, it calculates the offset to be added to the current buffer position, jumps there with i_d mode, and returns the result.",
      "summary": "The given C++ function generates jump instructions based on target addresses and modes, modifying buffer pointers accordingly. It calculates offsets for indirect jumps (GOTO, IFEQ) and array loads (ALOAD, FLOAD), as well as indirectly invoked special methods (INVOKESPECIAL). If the input mode is TARGET, it adds an offset to the current buffer position and jumps there with i_d mode before returning the result."
