    "BD2BCBAB95347999": {
      "code_hash": "f7002fcdf3f30bb7f724205c4d3ecbc4",
      "code_analysis": "This C++ function, `parse_fields`, parses the fields of a class or JNC (Java Native Interface) fields in a Korp object. It reads the bytes from the input buffer and determines if there are any JNC fields present within the class. If so, it iterates through them and adds their information to an array called `field_info`. Otherwise, it processes the non-JNC fields. For each field, it checks for a specific attribute value (\"ConstantValue\") and handles parsing of constant values if found; otherwise, it discards any unrecognized attributes. The function returns true when all fields have been processed and added to the `field_info` array.",
      "summary": "The `parse_fields` function/method primarily processes and parses fields within a class or JNC (Java Native Interface) fields within a Korp object. It determines if there are any JNC fields present, iterates through them, adds their information to an array called `field_info`, and handles parsing of constant values for non-JNC fields. This function aids in managing the structured data within the Korp object by providing an organized representation of its components."
